<title>AUSTRALIA: Clinton win encouraging for Australian farmer.</title>
<headline>Clinton win encouraging for Australian farmer.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>United States President Bill Clinton's election to a second term may be good news for Australian farmers, the National Farmers' Federation (NFF) said.</p>
<p>The chairman of NFF's economic committee, John Watson, said Clinton had begun a process of reducing subsidies for U.S. farmers through the Congressional Farm Bill earlier this year.</p>
<p>The NFF would like to see the Clinton reinforce this by dismantling the Export Enhancement Programme and the Dairy Export Incentive Programme, Watson said.</p>
<p>This was one of a number of issues NFF sought to discuss with Clinton during his Australia visit in November, he said.</p>
</text>
